) An explosion near a bus station in Gombe, Nigeria, killed at least five people and injured over a dozen, with witnesses describing a woman who placed an explosives-laden bag near a bus before fleeing and detonating it.  
) Although no group has claimed responsibility, Boko Haram is considered the main suspect, as the group has a history of targeting bus stations and markets, especially amid recent setbacks from regional offensives.  
) The attack occurred just after Nigeria's presidential election, which was won by Muhammadu Buhari, who has pledged to defeat Boko Haram.
